795199692, 'rerank_score': 5.035825729370117}, {'text': '[ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in]\nfunction ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in\n\nase.io.espresso. write_espresso_in ( fd , atoms , input_data = None , pseudopotentials = None , kspacing = None , kpts = None , koffset = (0, 0, 0) , crystal_coordinates = False , additional_cards = None , ** kwargs ) [source] #\n\nCreate an input file for pw.x.\n\nUse set_initial_magnetic_moments to turn on spin, if nspin is set to 2\nwith no magnetic moments, they will all be set to 0.0. Magnetic moments\nwill be converted to the QE units (fraction of valence electrons) using\nany pseudopotential files found, or a best guess for the number of\nvalence electrons.\n\nUnits are not converted for any other input data, so use Quantum ESPRESSO\nunits (Usually Ry or atomic units).\n\nKeys with a dimension (e.g. Hubbard_U(1)) will be incorporated as-is\nso the i should be made to match the output.\n\nImplemented features:', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/io/formatoptions.html#ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'write_espresso_in', 'class': None, 'function': 'write_espresso_in', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 5}, 'score': 4.679098129272461, 'vector_score': None, 'bm25_score': 39.15137745103975, 'rerank_score': 4.679098129272461}, {'text': '[ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_ph]\nAdditionally, a nat_todo_indices kwargs (list[int]) can be specified in the\nkwargs. It will be used if nat_todo is set to True in the input_data\ndictionary.\n\nGlobally, this function follows the convention set in the ph.x documentation\n( https://www.quantum-espresso.org/Doc/INPUT_PH.html )\n\nParameters : fd – The file descriptor of the input file. kwargs – kwargs dictionary possibly containing the following keys: input_data: dict qpts: list[list