xtxyz.read_extxyz]\nfunction ase.io.extxyz.read_extxyz\n\nase.io.extxyz. read_extxyz ( fileobj , index = -1 , properties_parser = <function key_val_str_to_dict> ) #\n\nRead from a file in Extended XYZ format\n\nindex is the frame to read, default is last frame (index=-1).\nproperties_parser is the parse to use when converting the properties line\nto a dictionary, extxyz.key_val_str_to_dict is the default and can\ndeal with most use cases, extxyz.key_val_str_to_dict_regex is slightly\nfaster but has fewer features.\n\nExtended XYZ format is an enhanced version of the basic XYZ format that allows extra\ncolumns to be present in the file for additonal per-atom properties as\nwell as standardising the format of the comment line to include the\ncell lattice and other per-frame parameters.', 'title': 'ase.io.extxyz.read_extxyz', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/io/formatoptions.html#ase.io.extxyz.read_extxyz', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.extxyz.read_extxyz', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'read_extxyz', 'class': None, 'function': 'read_extxyz', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 6}, 'score': -7.551252841949463, 'vector_score': 0.44323623180389404, 'bm25_score': None, 'rerank_score': -7.551252841949463}, {'text': '[ase.io.extxyz.read_extxyz]\nIt’s easiest to describe the format with an example. Here is a\nstandard XYZ file containing a bulk cubic 8 atom silicon cell\n\n```\n8\n\nCubic\n\nbulk\n\nsilicon\n\ncell\n\nSi\n\n0.00000000\n\n0.00000000\n\n0.00000000\n\nSi\n\n1.36000000\n\n1.36000000\n\n1.36000000\n\nSi\n\n2.72000000\n\n2.72000000\n\n0.00000000\n\nSi\n\n4.08000000\n\n4.08000000\n\n1.36000000\n\nSi\n\n2.72000000\n\n0.00000000\n\n2.72000000\n\nSi\n\n4.08000000\n\n1.36000000\n\n4.08000000\n\nSi\n\n0.00000000\n\n2.72000000\n\n2.72000000\n\nSi\n\n1.36000000\n\n4.08000000\n\n4.08000000\n```\n\nThe first line is the number of atoms, followed by a comment and\nthen one line per atom, giving the element symbol and cartesian\nx y, and z coordinates in Angstroms.\n\nHere’s the same configuration in extended XYZ format\n\n```\n8\n\nLattice\n=\n"5.44 0.0 0.0 0.0 5.44 0.0 0.0 0.0 5.44"\n\nProperties\n=\nspecies\n:\nS\n:\n1\n:\npos\n:\nR\n:\n3\n\nTime\n=\n0.0\n\nSi\n\n0.00000000\n\n0.00000000\n\n0.00000000\n\nSi', 'title': 'ase.io.extxyz.read_extxyz', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/io/formatoptions.html#ase.io.extxyz.read_extxyz', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.extxyz.read_extxyz', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'read_extxyz', 'class': None, 'function': 'read_extxyz', 'chunk_index': 1, 'num_chunks': 6}, 'score': -7.655351638793945, 'vector_score': 0.4552062451839447, 'bm25_score': None, 'rerank_score': -7.655351638793945}]}

